Terms:
Directory | file folder in device storage
Working directory | currently selected folder
CLI | Command Line Interface
options | optional addition(s) to a command that change what your result will be
arguments | optional addition(s) to a command (such as a file or path) to ensure the command has the correct content 

General Linux:
Linux is case sensitive - commands generally must be in lowercase letters
Options usually have a minus sign prior to it's symbol of choice (often a single lowercase letter or a short word describing its function
More than one option can be specified for a single command
Arguments are needed for certain commands and options, but not all of them. It has additional information for the command to operate on, such as a file or path
Command line format: $ command -options arguments | $ is the system prompt, command is the name of the command in use, -options is the minus symbol then the option designation (as applicable - not always needed), and arguments are the files names or path names (as applicable - not always needed)

